      "text": [
        " : سَأَلْتُهُ عَنِ اَلْمَرْأَةِ تَضْرِبُ عَلَيْهَا اَلظِّلاَلَ وَ هِيَ مُحْرِمَةٌ فَقَالَ «نَعَمْ» قُلْتُ فَالرَّجُلُ يَضْرِبُ عَلَيْهِ اَلظِّلاَلَ وَ هُوَ مُحْرِمٌ قَالَ «نَعَمْ إِذَا كَانَتْ بِهِ شَقِيقَةٌ وَ يَتَصَدَّقُ بِمُدٍّ لِكُلِّ يَوْمٍ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.2676 - Al-Bazanti narrated from Ali ibn Abi Hamzah, from Abu Basir, who said:\nI asked Imam (as) about a woman placing a shade over herself while she is in Ihram.\nImam (as) said: \"Yes.\"\nI asked: \"What about a man placing a shade over himself while in Ihram?\"\nImam (as) said: \"Yes, if he is afflicted with severe pain (shaqiqah), and he should give charity of a mudd for each day.\""
        ]
      }
    },
